(496104, 48526, 9146, '<td valign="top">At first I was tempted to coment that this dose not meet the challenge however your pic broght back a reminiss of childhood. Most easter sundays my Grandmother would buy me a new supper box of crayons. it would ber included in my basket with a colloring book that would take the place of the candy that would give me the uncontrolable sugar HADD''s I can remember the smell of all that fresh wax like it was yesterday.  This is so subtle but right on the money.<br/> <br/>as for the photography portion<br/> <br/>Negitive:<br/> <br/>Size too small<br/>When resizing in what ever program you use try making sure the largest side of your pic is at least 600 pixels long. There are several threads on this kind of thing. if you can''t find one post one of your own. wiser minds than mine can help you.<br/>Lack of sharpness <br/>You may want to try this on a tripod or some kind of stable surface but it looks like there was sufficint light to produce a sharp image. My sugestion is your focus is off. Try Macro mode if your camera has that feature.<br/>Blow out and bleed on the colors especaly the white crayon<br/>Try difusing the light some. I use drier sheets over my lights afixed with a embrodery hoop.Makes the house smell april fresh too.<br/> <br/>Positive:<br/>Very creative and subtle!!<br/>Wonderfull use of color<br/>Nice example of how to fill the frame<br/></td>', 'At first I was tempted to coment that this dose not meet the challenge however your pic broght back a reminiss of childhood. Most easter sundays my Grandmother would buy me a new supper box of crayons. it would ber included in my basket with a colloring book that would take the place of the candy that would give me the uncontrolable sugar HADD''s I can remember the smell of all that fresh wax like it was yesterday.  This is so subtle but right on the money. as for the photography portion Negitive: Size too smallWhen resizing in what ever program you use try making sure the largest side of your pic is at least 600 pixels long. There are several threads on this kind of thing. if you can''t find one post one of your own. wiser minds than mine can help you.Lack of sharpness You may want to try this on a tripod or some kind of stable surface but it looks like there was sufficint light to produce a sharp image. My sugestion is your focus is off. Try Macro mode if your camera has that feature.Blow out and bleed on the colors especaly the white crayonTry difusing the light some. I use drier sheets over my lights afixed with a embrodery hoop.Makes the house smell april fresh too. Positive:Very creative and subtle!!Wonderfull use of colorNice example of how to fill the frame', '2003-11-26 17:11:45.000000', NULL, 1),
