(497056, 48237, 11769, '<td valign="top">Very nice work here. so clear and wet looking I can almost smell the.... is that an orange or a lemon? well a 10 anywhey.</td>', 'Very nice work here. so clear and wet looking I can almost smell the.... is that an orange or a lemon? well a 10 anywhey.', '2003-11-27 18:34:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(497071, 48576, 2158, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done.  The shallow depth of field really works well here.</td>', 'Beautifully done.  The shallow depth of field really works well here.', '2003-11-27 19:03:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(497072, 48620, 11800, '<td valign="top">The colors and composition are very pleasing. Yes. My saliva glands are now open! Good job. The green background adds a nice touch.</td>', 'The colors and composition are very pleasing. Yes. My saliva glands are now open! Good job. The green background adds a nice touch.', '2003-11-27 19:05:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(497075, 48237, 7778, '<td valign="top">Exquisite.<br/> <br/>The crisp finesse of the arrangement is both apt and tangibly delicious. The various technical givens in this shot demonstrate a high degree of skill and accomplishment. <br/> <br/>For a photograph (and a studio shot at that) of this calibre I\''d prefer to see a more standard format, either vertical or horizontal, especially since there appears to be no compositional reason for the very static square.<br/> <br/>I rate this examplary image 8 (on a personal scale, mainly because of the limited range of both subject and topic). Within the context of DPC, it is a 10, no holds barred.</td>', 'Exquisite. The crisp finesse of the arrangement is both apt and tangibly delicious. The various technical givens in this shot demonstrate a high degree of skill and accomplishment.  For a photograph (and a studio shot at that) of this calibre I\''d prefer to see a more standard format, either vertical or horizontal, especially since there appears to be no compositional reason for the very static square. I rate this examplary image 8 (on a personal scale, mainly because of the limited range of both subject and topic). Within the context of DPC, it is a 10, no holds barred.', '2003-11-27 19:07:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(497076, 48562, 11800, '<td valign="top">Lighting and composition great. I think I would like to see more dof, but it''s your picture, so I guess you liked it that way.</td>', 'Lighting and composition great. I think I would like to see more dof, but it''s your picture, so I guess you liked it that way.', '2003-11-27 19:08:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(497083, 48441, 7778, '<td valign="top">Poor Van Gogh turning in his grave at the sight of such a thing. ;-) <br/> <br/>Not uninteresting. I enjoy the offset symmetry of shapes in this shot. A nearly balanced composition, if it weren''t for a slight vertical tilt to the left, which is emphasied by either or both lens distortion and form of the coffee maker. The crop. too, is quite tight, particularly top left.<br/> <br/>There seems to be some loss of detail in favour of some noise in the darker areas of the image. I am speculating that the ISO was above 200, instead of 100 or less, which would require the use of a tripod under darker conditions.</td>', 'Poor Van Gogh turning in his grave at the sight of such a thing. ;-)  Not uninteresting. I enjoy the offset symmetry of shapes in this shot. A nearly balanced composition, if it weren''t for a slight vertical tilt to the left, which is emphasied by either or both lens distortion and form of the coffee maker. The crop. too, is quite tight, particularly top left. There seems to be some loss of detail in favour of some noise in the darker areas of the image. I am speculating that the ISO was above 200, instead of 100 or less, which would require the use of a tripod under darker conditions.', '2003-11-27 19:25:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(497085, 48168, 11800, '<td valign="top">The leaves look splotchy.  I might have tried to focus on the tip of the front leaves and had a little more dof. Not trying to mean or anything.</td>', 'The leaves look splotchy.  I might have tried to focus on the tip of the front leaves and had a little more dof. Not trying to mean or anything.', '2003-11-27 19:27:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(497086, 47886, 11800, '<td valign="top">It''s a little too bright at the top but I like it. Mainly because that''s one of my favorite sayings when it comes to stink juice. I like your choice of dof except the dropper. I would have liked to see that sharp also.</td>', 'It''s a little too bright at the top but I like it. Mainly because that''s one of my favorite sayings when it comes to stink juice. I like your choice of dof except the dropper. I would have liked to see that sharp also.', '2003-11-27 19:31:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(497095, 48380, 2158, '<td valign="top">I wish you''d done this on a plainer background.  There are too many colours here that don''t seem to work together.</td>', 'I wish you''d done this on a plainer background.  There are too many colours here that don''t seem to work together.', '2003-11-27 19:49:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(497104, 47982, 11800, '<td valign="top">It''s beautiful. <br/>Trying to get an idea of how it was done. Lit from below and behind with flashes and a flashlight for the traces? How did you get an exposure long enough for the traces to be done? Slow shutter and the flash was delayed?</td>', 'It''s beautiful. Trying to get an idea of how it was done. Lit from below and behind with flashes and a flashlight for the traces? How did you get an exposure long enough for the traces to be done? Slow shutter and the flash was delayed?', '2003-11-27 20:05:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(497105, 48214, 11241, '<td valign="top">Very nice I love the image in the water</td>', 'Very nice I love the image in the water', '2003-11-27 20:05:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(497108, 47912, 10625, '<td valign="top">good idea, but lacks clarity.</td>', 'good idea, but lacks clarity.', '2003-11-27 20:09:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(497109, 47818, 11800, '<td valign="top">My mind keeps saying that this should be rotated 90 degrees clock-wise.  I don''t know. It doesn''t seem right but I can''t say anything other than that about the rotation.</td>', 'My mind keeps saying that this should be rotated 90 degrees clock-wise.  I don''t know. It doesn''t seem right but I can''t say anything other than that about the rotation.', '2003-11-27 20:11:33.000000', NULL, 1),
