(498720, 48511, 12809, '<td valign="top">Not a terribly bad photo, but it doesn''t do much for me.  The title doesn''t match the image.  This looks like a brand new candle that you lit, snapped one quick picture and immediately put out.  I don''t see any "Hot Candlewax".  Barely visible is a slight indentation where a bit of the candle melted.  The smoke is okay...but you can see the beginning and end of it and it again proves my theory of "light it, snap it, put it out".  The image also seems tilted too much CW.  A slight CCW rotation of this image would straighten it up nicely.  The black background is solid and nice.  Hope this helps.</td>', 'Not a terribly bad photo, but it doesn''t do much for me.  The title doesn''t match the image.  This looks like a brand new candle that you lit, snapped one quick picture and immediately put out.  I don''t see any "Hot Candlewax".  Barely visible is a slight indentation where a bit of the candle melted.  The smoke is okay...but you can see the beginning and end of it and it again proves my theory of "light it, snap it, put it out".  The image also seems tilted too much CW.  A slight CCW rotation of this image would straighten it up nicely.  The black background is solid and nice.  Hope this helps.', '2003-11-29 20:02:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(498724, 48466, 12809, '<td valign="top">This isn''t a bad photo but I''m not getting the idea of smell from it.  If it wasn''t for the title I would just see a photo of a mug.  What would help this, imo, is to take this from a higher angle to actually show the coffee inside (was there coffee even coffee in this mug?) and some hot steam would really add to it too.  Maybe a few coffee beans (like some others have done), a scoop of grinds, or a coffee pot or can of coffee blurred in the distance.  <br/> <br/>The lighting on the left of the mug is good but the right side of the mug is dark.  Also, this looks tilted CW too much.  You can really see it by looking at the background where the blue and white meet.  It goes downhill from left to right.<br/> <br/>Hope all of this helps...</td>', 'This isn''t a bad photo but I''m not getting the idea of smell from it.  If it wasn''t for the title I would just see a photo of a mug.  What would help this, imo, is to take this from a higher angle to actually show the coffee inside (was there coffee even coffee in this mug?) and some hot steam would really add to it too.  Maybe a few coffee beans (like some others have done), a scoop of grinds, or a coffee pot or can of coffee blurred in the distance.   The lighting on the left of the mug is good but the right side of the mug is dark.  Also, this looks tilted CW too much.  You can really see it by looking at the background where the blue and white meet.  It goes downhill from left to right. Hope all of this helps...', '2003-11-29 20:13:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(498725, 48206, 12809, '<td valign="top">Quite a simple shot, really, but I like it!  I like the border too.  The colors and sharpness are good.  Nice job.  I gave this an 8.</td>', 'Quite a simple shot, really, but I like it!  I like the border too.  The colors and sharpness are good.  Nice job.  I gave this an 8.', '2003-11-29 20:20:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(498728, 48577, 12809, '<td valign="top">Pretty simple idea, but it looks very nice.  I like the use of artifial snow.  There seems to be a hint of yellow in the white of the candy canes in the top left.  See how much whiter the ones in the bottom right are?  Must be something with the lighting.  I gave this an 8, though.</td>', 'Pretty simple idea, but it looks very nice.  I like the use of artifial snow.  There seems to be a hint of yellow in the white of the candy canes in the top left.  See how much whiter the ones in the bottom right are?  Must be something with the lighting.  I gave this an 8, though.', '2003-11-29 20:21:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(498732, 48562, 12809, '<td valign="top">Love it!  Love this shot too.  :-)  Good color, sharpness and layout.  Like how you brought a few cloves away.  Kind of wish the entire image was in focus.  That bottom left corner keeps pulling my eye to it.  Nice work.  I gave this an 8.</td>', 'Love it!  Love this shot too.  :-)  Good color, sharpness and layout.  Like how you brought a few cloves away.  Kind of wish the entire image was in focus.  That bottom left corner keeps pulling my eye to it.  Nice work.  I gave this an 8.', '2003-11-29 20:23:49.000000', NULL, 1),
